name issue_466_undershoot_1mbps
describe 1 Mbps link, an encoder whose delta frames are 0.7x its target
duration 40s
encoder_overshoot 0.7
at 0s capacity=1mbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
# Issue #466 (see issue_466_overshoot_1mbps.scn). With overshoot 1 the encoder
# target is 788-800 kbps and the encoded rate 795-805 kbps (seeds 1-3); at 0.7
# the encoded rate falls to 623-703 kbps and the adjuster's media utilization
# (RateUtilizationTracker) raises the target to 882-1006 kbps.
expect video.avg_kbps < 750
# #517 (RTCP interval draws seeded as libwebrtc's): seed 1 reads 831.6 (main 882; seeds 1-10 mean 942 -> 929,
# 831.6-1007). libwebrtc has no column for this metric: for the Coordinator to judge (program.md 0.2).
expect video.encoder_target_avg_kbps > 830
